# --- end vendor verification

external:        Operating system permissions on the persistent queue files when
                 outputs.conf persistentQueueSize is set, since data staged on disk before
                 transmission is protected by the file system rather than by the
                 application
external:        The receiving indexer's own TLS configuration, which completes the
                 protected channel
external:        The SMTP relay's TLS support, which determines whether the email alert
                 action uses implicit TLS or STARTTLS
external:        Certificate authority and key material placed on the host per
                 SPLK-CL-000450

citation:        SRG-APP-000441-WSR-000181 check text; SPLK-CL-000460 fix text;
                 SPLK-CL-000430 fix text; outputs.conf.spec:160-175, 345-360, 647-712,
                 779-791, 832-855; alert_actions.conf.spec:287-300, 428-450
finding:         Data staged for transmission leaves Splunk without the protection the
                 product can apply: the [tcpout:<group>] output lacks a client certificate,
                 does not pin sslVersions to tls1.2, does not verify the receiver's
                 certificate or does not use indexer acknowledgment, or the email alert
                 action does not verify the SMTP server's certificate on an approved TLS
                 version.
